BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Photo Editing with Photoshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260615T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260615T190000
UID:6a021a438e677a28001b4b09@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Adobe Photoshop is the world’s best imaging and graphic desi
 gn software and is at the core of just about every creative project\, from
  photo editing and compositing to digital painting\, animation\, and graph
 ic design.\nJoin us for an introductory lesson and learn about the most co
 mmon tools. We'll explore the workspace and enhance images while investiga
 ting tools such as crop\, levels\, colour balance and more. See how an ima
 ge can be altered and repaired using patch tools such as the clone and hea
 ling brush tools. We'll also dive deep into the world of layers and how yo
 u can manage them for those really unique and fun projects.\nRegistration 
 is required.\nPlease be noted that your spot will be taken by others if yo
 u failed to show up 5 mins after class begins.\nInformation Collection Not
 ice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pu
 blic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and
  20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrati
 on\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your
  information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\,
  416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fairview\, DIH\, 3rd floor\, Fairview Branch
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a021a438e677a28001b4b09
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
